{
    "_about": [
        "National distinctions: the score to reach for each badge, by discipline, bow and age class.",
        "Source: federation general rules, chapter F.2 (edition February 2023), and the badge poster (May 2024).",
        "A discipline holds one or more sets (families of badges: Marcassins, Ecureuils...).",
        "columns: the score columns of the set. bows = the ianseo division codes of the column (beware: in 3D",
        "  and nature, CL is the barebow and CO the bare compound); ages = the age classes allowed (all when",
        "  absent); text = written on the badge, one text or one per age class (then only these classes earn it);",
        "  layers = looks.json layers the column adds (compound: the cam); tile = border of the text tiles.",
        "levels: in order, from the first badge to the last; each column name gives the score to reach.",
        "  badge = family of looks.json (a drawn picture); without it the level shows as a text tile.",
        "  face = diameter of the target face (cm) required for that level, when the rules require one.",
        "measure: what is compared to the threshold, score (default) or honours (beursault: arrows that hit)."
    ],
